; Low from a pair. Winning 42 p. 49 (S-0071-c); the 84 form p. 70
; (S-0097-c); played in Hand 35 (S-0151-e, S-0151-h).
; Rule, in our words: a setter following a suit, whoever led it, in which he
; holds exactly two tiles, neither of them count, plays the lower and keeps the
; higher. Against a bid of marks, where count no longer matters and every
; trick does, he keeps two tiles of the suit of the bidder's double to the end:
; he plays the lower on the double, count or not, and keeps the higher for the
; off.
; Scope: the book's pair is kept for a later lead of the suit; it does not
; treat the case where the higher tile takes a trick the bidder's side is
; taking (the catalog's note on S-0071-c). There the first rule does not fire
; (2026-10-14, #146; before, it played low and gave the trick away). The
; book's general "win any trick you can" (S-0056-b) is not encoded for a
; follower who is not last (GAPS.md, the book's silences).
; Replaces gates/c13c-low-from-a-pair.silas. How it differs: the first rule is
; the gate's (the book's leader is anyone, as the gate already reads it). The
; 84 form is new: the gate needs a pair without count, so it is silent where
; the book plays low from a pair that holds a count tile.
; The spare: in Hand 29 trick 3 (S-0133-j) the right setter holds the 6-1 and
; the 3-1 on his partner's 1-0; the book says either will do and plays the
; higher, the 6-1, "because you have another six". Re-read 2026-10-14 (#153),
; presuming the encoding misread: the pair rule keeps the higher for a later
; lead of the suit followed; here the aces are dead (the 1-1 has just won
; the trick) and each ace belongs to another suit besides. The 3-1 with the
; 5-3 is a pair in treys that catches the 3-0 still out (pair-targets.silas);
; the 6-1 is spare, since the 6-6 in his hand already cannot lose the sixes.
; The condition the rule omitted is the book's own reason: with two followers
; of a pair, neither count, play the one whose other suit a tile of yours
; already holds, and keep the one that keeps a pair. Before, the rule allowed
; only the 3-1 there.

(include book)

(policy low-from-a-pair
  (rule keep-the-pair-play-the-spare (play spare)
    (roles me spare kept led)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (not (every-trick))
    (led-context led)
    (not (trump led))
    (follower spare)
    (count spare 0)
    (follower kept)
    (count kept 0)
    (none (roles third) (follower third) (not (tile third spare)) (not (tile third kept)))
    (none (roles w win)
      (current-winner w)
      (opponent me w)
      (trick-play w win)
      (or (beats spare win led) (beats kept win led)))
    (keeps-a-pair kept)
    (not (keeps-a-pair spare))
    (some (roles held r)
      (mine held)
      (not (tile held spare))
      (not (tile held kept))
      (not (in held led))
      (in spare r)
      (in held r)
      (not (can-lose held))))
  (rule follow-low (play low)
    (roles me low high led)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (led-context led)
    (not (trump led))
    (follower low)
    (count low 0)
    (follower high)
    (count high 0)
    (beats high low led)
    (none (roles w win) (current-winner w) (opponent me w) (trick-play w win) (beats high win led))
    (none (roles third) (follower third) (not (tile third low)) (not (tile third high))))
  (rule keep-the-higher-for-the-off (play low)
    (roles me doubled low high led)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (every-trick)
    (bidder-led doubled)
    (double doubled)
    (led-context led)
    (not (trump led))
    (follower low)
    (follower high)
    (beats high low led)
    (none (roles third) (follower third) (not (tile third low)) (not (tile third high)))))
